   832                              <1> ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
   833                              <1> ; A character can pop a cell or two too many, or push one too many, before
   834                              <1> ; it is seen here: the data stack has the caller's frame above it and the
   835                              <1> ; thread's stack below, and the return stack has the image's spare space on
   836                              <1> ; both sides.
